A||N||5||rockcrawl||What happened to Zumalt's supercharged Northstar?||||10||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||01-17-2001||07:38 PM||||I was wondering if anyone knows what happened to the supercharged Northstar that Gary Zumalt built. Was it ever installed in a car? It must have been pretty awesome! Here are a few pics of it mounted on a Fiero cradle, notice Gary in the backround.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zumalt2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zumalt1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Will||01-18-2001||10:39 AM||||Where did you get these pictures?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||01-18-2001||11:09 AM||||i'd have to look, but i'm sure i saw a picture of a s/c northstar in one of the kit car mags, in an article about swaps. nothing really said about it beyond that it was in there. you could see the s/c on top though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||01-18-2001||03:41 PM||||The first pic was taken at the 12th Annual FOCOA Fiero Festival in Indianapolis, Aug 1996. It was sacanned from Fiero Owner 3rd quarter '96. The second is from one of Gary Zumalt's V-8 conversion ads from about the same time. The ad mentioned nothing about the Northstar, only big and small block chevys.<BR> <BR> It appears the engine is still fuel injected too. Those look like Cadillac MPFI throttle bodies on top. Must have been a challenge to get a program to run that.<P>I did get to meet Gary at the Carlisle show a few years back when he was still doing conversions. But at that time I was more interested in Lambo rebodies than V-8 Fieros.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
